    "body": "Problem:\r\n`nvim --embed --listen addr` always treats stdin as an RPC channel. If\r\nstdin is /dev/null (e.g. backgrounded over ssh), the channel closes\r\nbefore a UI can attach, so Nvim exits (detach=false behavior). If stdin\r\nis a tty, keystrokes are read as RPC.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nWith `--embed --listen`, open the stdio RPC channel only if stdin is\r\na pipe or socket. Else wait for a UI at the `--listen` address.\r\n\r\n    $ nvim --embed --listen ./nvim.sock\r\n    Nvim server (pid: 71984) waiting for UI, listening on: \"./nvim.sock\"\r\n\r\nNote:\r\n- No change when stdin is a pipe. So the test harness, TUI, and :restart\r\n  all behave exactly as before.\r\n- The #29634 use-case of configuring a UI that attaches *after* startup\r\n  (a second UI, or reattach) still requires #25377 (reliable UIEnter).\r\n  Not affected by this change.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/29634\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/38456",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-09T16:44:29Z",
